BSD diff writes a file name with a newline unquoted, which splits the header.

Command: diff -u x 'y
y'
Tool: Apple diff (based on FreeBSD diff)
-- x --
a
-- y --
b
-- diff --
--- x	2026-01-02 03:04:05
+++ y
y	2026-01-02 03:04:06
@@ -1 +1 @@
-a
+b
-- error --
line 3: missing hunk header after file header
